        <item>
            <title>0.13.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:33:24 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>367</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.13.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
  <li><strong>Drop a whole wedding at once.</strong> Import a folder and Supply sorts it into cameras for you — A-Cam, B-Cam, Drone, whatever your cards are named.</li>
  <li><strong>Browse camera by camera.</strong> Each camera gets its own view, so you can work through one card at a time instead of scrolling past every clip from the day.</li>
  <li><strong>Categorize and grade per camera.</strong> Run either one on just the camera you're in, and the toolbar shows which camera it's working on.</li>
  <li><strong>Better relinking.</strong> If footage moves, Supply is smarter about reconnecting each clip to the right file, even when two cameras have a clip with the same name.</li>
  <li>Tidied up the export and categorize progress bars in the toolbar.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
